<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;"><span style="font-family:Tomaha,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;">Dear,<br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="line-height:115%"><span lang="EN-US">In reviewing your Publicly Funded IVF Program application (</span></span></span></span>{{{Case.CaseNumber}}}<span style="font-family:Tomaha,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="line-height:115%"><span lang="EN-US">), a discrepancy was noted between information on your Medical Services Plan (MSP) account and your application.</span></span></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="line-height:115%"><span lang="EN-CA">It is important to keep your Medical Services Plan (MSP) account up-to-date, as some changes may affect your coverage. If your family unit has changed, you must update your Medical Services Plan (MSP) account. Please visit the MSP website for more details </span><a href="https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/health/health-drug-coverage/msp/bc-residents/managing-your-msp-account" style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; color:blue; text-decoration:underline">gov.bc.ca/managingyourmspaccount</a><span lang="EN-CA">. If you have questions regarding your MSP account please Contact Health Insurance BC </span><a href="https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/health/health-drug-coverage/msp/bc-residents-contact-us" style="font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif; color:blue; text-decoration:underline">https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/health/health-drug-coverage/msp/bc-residents-contact-us</a><span lang="EN-CA">.&nbsp;</span></span></span><br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="line-height:115%"><span lang="EN-CA">This does not impact your application and you are encouraged to remain in contact with your fertility clinic regarding your application status. </span></span></span><br />
<br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:12pt"><span style="line-height:normal"><span lang="EN-CA">Sincerely,</span></span></span><br />
